hey everyone its Johanna here and always  emphasize how important it is to have  your breakfast in the morning to kick  start your day and I know it can be  difficult especially for those of us who  are busy and the last thing we want to  think about is to make a healthy  breakfast so I've decided to share with  you some of my really easy  make-ahead breakfast which you can prep  over the weekends and this will last you  the entire week this are all really  simple ingredients really quick to make  give it a smell and the look of it right  now it's making me hungry and they would  definitely brighten up your entire week  let's start with my favorite make-ahead  breakfast which is my egg muffin this  egg muffin a packed full of protein from  the egg and the chicken roll I've used  and also you're getting some vegetables  that you need as well as the cheese on  top of it they're so adorable so easy to  eat and each one of them only has one  hundred and twenty three point five  calories so if you like savory food for  your breakfast or if you like to have  eggs in your breakfast this is for you  the ingredients you need are 6 4 X 5  finely sliced chicken rolls or ham or  even any other protein that you prefer  50 gram of kale or spinach or other  leafy vegetables 20 grams of grated  cheese 40 grams of carrots finely slice  again choose another vegetables that you  like such as tomatoes and 1 TSP of olive  oil the first step is to lightly stir  fry your kale and carrots until softened  for about 5 minutes  then add your chicken roll mix them all  up and remove the mix ingredients from  the heat in the meantime  pre-heat your oven to 180  of 350 farenheit next step whisk six  whole eggs get a muffin tray and  transfer your mixed vegetables  ingredients into the muffin tray evenly  once that's done pour your egg mixture  into the muffin tray and just top it up  with your grated cheese all you'll need  to do now is to place your muffin tray  into the oven for 10 minutes and you'll  have your egg muffin and here is your  protein pack and muffin what I tend to  do is to pack those up individually in  an aluminum foil and place them in the  freezer every morning just take them out  remove them from the foil and just warm  them up in the microwave and you have  your breakfast ready it is as simple as  that so try it out  if you like to have pastries bread  scones muffins for breakfast then this  is for you what I have here are banana  muffins you don't have to use bananas  you can choose any other of your  favorite fruits the great thing about  this recipe is that there is no flour  and there is no added sugar at all so  they are basically packed with healthy  ingredients to kickstart your day the  ingredients you need are to the cup of  oats which is about 60 grow to medium  very ripe bananas meshed 1/2 cup of  unsweetened applesauce which is about  243 grab 2 large eggs 1/2 a cup of Greek  yogurt which is about 125 gram 1  teaspoon of vanilla extract 1 tablespoon  of baking powder quarter teaspoon of  baking soda 45 gram of coarsely chopped  almond nuts or any other nuts seeds or  dried fruits of your choice so the first  step is to mix the dry ingredients  together so add your oats baking powder  baking soda and almond nuts into a bowl  and just mix them all up the second step  is to add your wet ingredients so  measure bananas up mix it up with Greek  yogurt break 2 large eggs and continue  to mix it add your applesauce and  finally add one teaspoon of vanilla  extract and make sure they're all evenly  mixed then combine your dry ingredients  with your wet ingredients and mix them  all up evenly  in the meantime pre-heat your oven to  200 degrees Celsius or 400 degrees  Fahrenheit spray the bottom of the  muffin cup with a little bit of cooking  spray to avoid the banana muffin from  sticking finally transfer the mixture  into charm muffin cups allow it to cook  in the oven for 15 minutes once it's  cooked remove it and let it cool for 10  minutes so here are your banana muffins  for the entire week you can place half  of this in the freezer and another half  you can store them into a container and  place them in the fridge  this banana muffins are really soft and  moist but you're getting the crunchiness  from the nuts and each of them only has  105 calories so you can choose to have  to fear breakfast or you can mix them up  have one banana muffin and one egg  muffin if you're really in a rush  you can always pack them and bring it  out with you and have it on the way to  school all work I tend to cook oats in  the morning and have them for my  breakfast but if you don't have the time  try this out this is an overnight OT  yogurt parfait there is no cooking  required it's just basically assembling  your boat  yogurt and your fruits store it in the  fridge and it's ready to be eaten the  next day it's refreshing and it would  definitely fill you up the ingredients  you need are half the cup of Greek  yogurt which is about 125 grams 1/3 cup  of oats which is about 30 gram 2 tbsp of  milk I use soya milk which is about 30  ml 1 cup of frozen berries which is  about 150 gram or any other fresh fruits  of your choice and half a tablespoon of  mixed seeds so what we want to do is to  mix the Greek yogurt oats milk and mix  it into a bowl and now it's time to  assemble your ot yogurt parfait  you can choose to paste it in a jar  which will last you up to 5 days or you  can place it in a cup just like what I'm  doing so the first layer is to place  your yogurt mixture add your frozen  berries place another layer of yogurt  mixture and finally as your frozen  berries and just place it into the  fridge when you leave it in the fridge  overnight what happens is that the  frozen yogurt with all and  the sweetness of the berries will sit  into the yogurt and into the oats as  well so what you'll have is a really  creamy texture with lots of natural  sweetness coming from the berries if you  have a really busy day ahead and you  don't have time for snack like your  breakfast hub with ingredients that will  keep you satisfied unto lunchtime and  finally the breakfast that is highly  sugar which will boosts your energy and  lift your mood up this chewy energy bars  are only made with three ingredients 1  cup of pitted dates which is about 150  gram 1 cup of raisins or any other dried  fruits which is also about 150 gram one  cut off two core cashew nuts or any  other preferred nuts which is about 140  gram all you'll need to do is place  these three ingredients into the food  processor and grind them if you have a  really powerful food processor you will  have a really fine mixture my mixture is  rather coarse but that's fine the next  step is to place your sticky mixture  onto a thin layer of plastic and just  press it down and make a large block  once you have a nice large block slice  it up into 10 smaller blocks and stack  them up by separating them with a thin  layer of plastic these energy bars are  really soft and chewy packed full of  natural sugar so if you feel down or low  in energy and you need a quick sugar  rush choose these snack bars instead of  any other chunks each one of these bars  has 183 degrees this cheery snack bars  can be stored in your food cupboard or  you can store them in the fridge again  feel free to mix and match your  breakfast so take the time over the  weekends buy the ingredients you need  decide which breakfast you would like to  make make them store them in the fridge  or in the freezer take them out the next  day  warm them up and you have  your healthy breakfast to kick-start  your day this breakfast will give you  lots of energy it's good to your body  and you will put a smile on your face so  try them out let me know what you think  in the comments below for new Fitness  food and motivational videos please like  share and subscribe to my You Tube  channel and website do follow me on  Facebook Instagram and Twitter to stay  connected with me thanks guys  you
 

